{{#if isGraphQL}}---
description: GraphQL Object Type Guidelines  
globs: "**/*.object.ts"
alwaysApply: true
---
- Use `@ObjectType()` decorator for all GraphQL output types
{{#if isMongoose}}- Always implement the standard constructor pattern to handle MongoDB documents:
  ```ts
  constructor(input: EntityDocument | EntityObject) {
    Object.assign(this, {
      ...((input as any)._doc
        ? (input as EntityDocument).toObject({ virtuals: true })
        : input),
    });
  }
  ```
- This pattern ensures proper handling of virtual fields like `id` vs `_id`{{/if}}
- This should expose properties from {{#if isMongoose}}`<entity>.schema.ts`{{/if}}{{#if isPrisma}}Prisma schema{{/if}} file, without properties which shouldn't be exposed like password hash, and other which are not needed for client to use, and just for proper handling on backend
@object-template.ts{{/if}}
